index 52dad963..00000000
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/394-wifi-mac80211-select-the-link-a-management-frame-asks.patch
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,69 +0,0 @@
-From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
-Date: Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: select the link a management frame asks for
-
-ieee80211_mgmt_tx() walks the links of an AP MLD to decide whether the
-frame needs an off-channel transmission. It pins the link to the one
-that holds the requested channel only when the destination is a station
-that is already associated as an MLD. A frame to an address the access
-point does not know keeps link_id at -1.
-
-ieee80211_tx_skb_tid_band() then sees a frame whose transmitter address
-is the MLD address and marks the link as IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_MLO_LINK
-unspecified. The driver picks the default link, which is not the link
-that holds the requested channel. mt7996 rewrites addr2 with the address
-of that link and hands the frame to its phy, so the frame leaves on the
-wrong band under the wrong address.
-
-A DPP Authentication Request shows this. The enrollee announces itself
-on channel 6, the access point answers on the 5 GHz link, and the
-enrollee never sees the frame.
-
-The channel the caller names identifies the link on its own. Pin the
-link whenever the frame comes from the MLD address and an active link
-holds that channel, whether or not the destination is a known station.
-ieee80211_tx_skb_tid() warns on a link id for an interface that is not
-an MLD and on one that names an inactive link, and active_links is zero
-for an interface that is not an MLD, so that one test covers both. The
-same holds for a station MLD that sends from its MLD address to an
-address other than its AP.
-
-A link whose own address is the MLD address matched the frame on that
-address first and ended the search, so the link with the requested
-channel was never reached when a lower link uses the MLD address. Skip
-such a link when the frame names another channel.
-
-Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
