-From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
-Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: retransmit the 4-address null frame until
- it is acknowledged
-
-A station in 4-address mode sends one 4-address null data frame after
-association, or when 4-address mode is enabled while it is associated.
-The access point sets up the 4-address station only when it receives
-that frame. If the frame is lost, the access point keeps the station in
-3-address mode.
-
-If the driver reports ACK status, request TX status for the frame and
-send it again every second until the access point acknowledges it, for
-at most ten transmissions, so that a driver that loses the TX status of
-the frame does not keep it going for the whole association. The
-retransmission stops on disassociation, when 4-address mode is
-disabled, and when the interface stops. A hardware restart keeps the
-association, so it does not stop the retransmission.
-
-The TX status path runs without the wiphy mutex and cannot cancel the
-delayed work. It records the ACK instead, and the work then does
-nothing.
-
-Based on 0089-mtk-mac80211-retransmit-4addr-nullfunc-if-the-ACK-is.patch
-by Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com> in the MediaTek feed. That
-patch uses status type 3, which is IEEE80211_STATUS_TYPE_UHR_OMP here,
-and cancels the work from the TX status path.
-
-Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
