-From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
-Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:23:37 +0200
-Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: report the MLD address and link of a dumped
- station
-
-Since nl80211_dump_station() builds the aggregated message with
-nl80211_put_sta_info_common() instead of nl80211_send_station(), a
-station dump no longer carries NL80211_ATTR_MLD_ADDR and
-NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID, while NL80211_CMD_GET_STATION for one station
-still does. Userspace that dumps the stations of an AP MLD can then no
-longer tell an MLO station from a legacy one, nor its association link.
-
-Move the MLO parameters into nl80211_put_sta_mlo_params() and emit them
-in the aggregated message of the dump as well. The association IEs stay
-out of the dump, as 727afb05ef63 intends.
-
-Fixes: 727afb05ef63 ("wifi: cfg80211: Refactor nl80211_dump_station() to prepare for per-link stats")
-Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
