--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/419-wifi-mac80211_hwsim-report-the-TX-counters-and-rate-of-each-station-link.patch
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,216 +0,0 @@
-From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
-Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:44:19 +0200
-Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211_hwsim: report the TX counters and rate of each
- station link
-
-mac80211 books every frame to an MLO station on the default link, so a
-per-link station dump shows all TX bytes, packets and the TX rate on the
-association link, and none on the other links, whichever link carried
-the frames. Userspace that compares the links of a station, for example
-to report the metrics of each affiliated station, then reads wrong
-values.
-
-hwsim selects the link of each frame. Count the bytes and packets per
-access category on that link as ieee80211_tx_h_stats() counts them on
-the default link: the length before encryption, and one packet for all
-fragments of an MSDU. Record the rate of the first attempt of a data
-frame with the band of the link channel. A frame whose link station is
-not resolved is not counted. Report bytes, packets and rate from the
-link_sta_statistics callback, which mac80211 calls for each link of a
-station with links. Retries, failures and the other per-link fields stay
-mac80211's.
-
-Clear the record of a link that is new to the station's valid links.
-old_links and new_links of change_sta_links are masked with the active
-links, so a link that becomes active again keeps its record. A record
-also starts again for a new link station under the same link ID, since
-mac80211 does not call change_sta_links for a link it removes after the
-vif link or for a dormant one.
-
-The rate is the rate at TX time, not the rate of the TX status, which
-names no link; with HAS_RATE_CONTROL the two are the same here. The
-station totals are the sum of the links, and of removed links, whose
-counters mac80211 now takes from the driver.
-
-Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
